<article class="env-lemma" id="0GMC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GMC">Lemma <span data-tag="0GMC">67.49.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then for $x \in |X|$ we have: $x$ has codimension $0$ in $X \Rightarrow f(x)$ has codimension $0$ in $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Via Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BAQ" data-tag="0BAQ">66.11.1</a> and étale localization this translates into the case of a morphism of schemes and generic points of irreducible components. Here the result follows as generalizations lift along flat morphisms of schemes, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/03HV" data-tag="03HV">29.26.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>